 "spec_id": "var-kp_vy-vym6-v1",
 "title": "KP14 vym3 at K = 6: SIX priced OU states at total price 2.5 (2.5/sqrt(6) each), 24 types with rank-6 loading vectors (six alignments x four magnitudes), level-compensated",
 "question": "Does raising the number of priced states past the number of characteristics (five) open room that K = 3 (vym3: room 19% of linear, gap -0.003) did not?",
 "notes": "WHY (2026-10-27). The campaign's gaps are small because every economy gives the linear sort a NONZERO correlation with the priced exposure: with one priced factor and N = 500, any such portfolio mimics the factor and diversifies the rest, so it earns the factor's whole Sharpe ratio however curved the exposure is (the 2026-10-26 reduced-form sign screen: room is all or nothing). Room needs the exposure to be orthogonal to every linear function of the characteristics -- in the cross-section (a hidden sign: vyg25s, room 0.35, gap +0.18) or in time (a premium whose sign the constant-weight portfolio cannot follow). vym3's content is the product of magnitude ||b_f|| (which the characteristics reveal) and alignment b_f . gamma / ||b_f|| (which they do not). The 2026-10-11 reduced-form K ladder found room and gap rising with the number of priced factors; K = 6 is the first structural point past the five characteristics, built EXACTLY as vym3 (same magnitudes, alignments spread over the same range, total price 2.5) so that only K moves. Six alignments fit six mutually orthogonal directions in the complement of gamma, which K = 3 could not give vym3's five.\n\nFEASIBILITY: no product grid -- each type is the scalar problem at its own projection (parameters_kp14 'several priced states'); 24 G-stage types then the integ tables, about twice vym3's build.\n\nPRECOMMITMENT STATUS: precommitted=false; ids filled from the Quest build log by the solve script before any seed runs.\n\nPREDICTION (2026-10-27): room above vym3's 19% of the linear ceiling, 25-35%; fair gap between -0.005 and +0.02, direction not called (vym3's room went unlearned). FALSIFIED as 'K past the characteristic count opens room' if room is at or below 19%.",
